===== FILE: docs/SYNC-SPEC.md =====
# Heldnote Drive Sync — v2 Specification (draft for adversarial review)

## Goal
Replace the one-way Drive *backup* (single snapshot, restore-as-copies) with
**two-way sync** so a user editing on phone and PC sees the same notes on both,
without ever violating the product promise: *nothing you type is ever lost*.

## Non-goals
- No server, no CRDTs, no realtime. Drive appDataFolder stays the only transport.
- Manual file export/import (exportAll/importAll) stays exactly as is.
- No per-keystroke sync; note-level granularity is enough.

## Current state (what changes)
- drive-sync.js uploads `heldnote-backup.json` = full exportAll() snapshot,
  debounced 30s / max once per 5min. Restore = importAll('copy'|'replace').
- Notes already carry: id, createdAt, updatedAt, localRev, pinned,
  isDeleted/deletedAt (trash), and an immutable version history (seq, at,
  sourceRev, text). purgeNote() deletes the record entirely (no tombstone).

## Design

### Local additions (store.js + meta store)
- `deviceId`: random UUID, persisted in meta once.
- Per-note sync state in meta: `sync:<noteId>` = { syncedAt, syncedUpdatedAt,
  syncedTextHash } written after each successful sync. Used to answer "has this
  side changed since the last sync?" (three-way merge base).
- Tombstones: purgeNote()/emptyTrash record `{ id, purgedAt }` in a meta
  tombstone list (retention 180 days) so purges propagate instead of the
  purged note resurrecting from the other device.

### Sync file (Drive appDataFolder)
`heldnote-sync.json` = { schemaVersion, syncFormat: 2, deviceId, syncedAt,
notes: [as exportAll], versions: [as exportAll], tombstones: [{id, purgedAt}],
meta: settings subset }. The legacy `heldnote-backup.json` is still written
opportunistically after a successful sync (cheap: same payload minus sync
fields) so old clients/manual restore keep working; it is never read by sync.

### Merge algorithm (runs under withGlobalLock, after the flush phase — same
lock discipline as exportAll: flush OUTSIDE the lock, merge INSIDE)
1. Download `heldnote-sync.json`. Missing → upload local state, done.
2. For each note id in union(local, remote, tombstones):
   - Tombstone newer than both sides' updatedAt → purge locally, keep tombstone.
   - Only local → keep, will be uploaded.
   - Only remote (no tombstone) → import note + its versions.
   - Both, syncedTextHash matches both → no-op.
   - Remote changed since base, local unchanged → apply remote fields + text;
     union version histories (dedupe by (at, sourceRev, textHash)).
   - Local changed, remote unchanged since base → keep local.
   - **Both changed (true conflict)** → last-writer-wins by updatedAt for the
     live text/fields, and the losing text is committed as a history version
     first (so it is one tap away in History, never lost). Union histories.
   - Trash state (isDeleted/deletedAt) merges by the same LWW rule; a trashed
     note is still synced (trash is visible on both devices).
3. Write merged state locally (single transaction batch; additive semantics —
   no record is dropped except via tombstone rule).
4. Upload merged file. Race guard: capture the remote file's modifiedTime at
   download; before PATCH, re-fetch metadata; if modifiedTime changed, another
   device synced meanwhile → re-run merge from step 1 (max 3 attempts, then
   surface quiet "sync-conflict, will retry" status).
5. Update per-note sync meta + lastSyncAt.

### Never-lose invariants (reviewers: try to break these)
- A fresh/empty device with an existing remote file must PULL, never clobber
  (replaces today's refused-empty guard — now it just merges, empty side
  contributes nothing).
- Every text that was ever the live text of a note on any device survives —
  as live text or as a history version.
- Offline/401/quota mid-sync leaves local state exactly as before merge began
  (merge is computed fully, then applied; apply is transactional per phase).
- Version history byte budgets (constants.js) still apply after union — prune
  by existing maintenance rules, never below "conflict loser" snapshots newer
  than 7 days.

### Triggers
- App load (silent, only with fresh token), visibilitychange→visible (throttled),
  after durable saves via existing noteSaved debounce (30s / 5min unchanged),
  manual "Sync now" button.

### UI (notes-ui.js + i18n)
- Drive panel: "Backup now"/"Restore" → "Sync now" + status line
  ("Synced ✓ 12:41", "Sync failed — will retry", "Sign in to resume sync").
- No conflict dialogs. Conflicts resolve silently; History carries the loser.
- All new strings in i18n.js for every SUPPORTED language.

### Files
- NEW `sync-engine.js`: pure merge logic (unit-testable, no IO).
- drive-sync.js: file v2 up/download, sync loop, race guard, triggers.
- store.js: importMergeBatch(), tombstone recording, sync meta helpers,
  commitConflictVersion().
- notes-ui.js, i18n.js: UI + strings. tests/sync.test.js: merge engine tests
  (pure, runs in existing browser harness).

## Acceptance criteria
1. Edit note on A, sync A, sync B → B shows A's text; no duplicates.
2. Edit same note on both, sync A then B then A → both converge to the newer
   text; older text present in History on both.
3. Trash on A propagates to B; purge on A removes on B via tombstone; restored-
   from-trash on B after A's trash wins if later (LWW).
4. Fresh browser + existing remote → full library appears; nothing uploaded
   until merge completes.
5. Kill the tab mid-sync at any await point → reload loses nothing.
6. Legacy heldnote-backup.json alone (no sync file) → first sync imports it
   as the remote baseline instead of ignoring existing backups.
